I wrote two task files and the issue responses to session_plan/. The commit step did nothing: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The plan's commit command ends in || true, which suggests the harness reads the files from disk anyway. If it needs them committed, they'd have to be added with git add -f.

Task 1 (product): Part of #1023. Two false statements left over from the search/list_files fence:
• Footer count: when the fence withholds lines, the search footer (N matches) still counts them. It should count only what was shown. Output must stay byte-identical when nothing is withheld, and that gets a test plus a sabotage check.
• Docs: docs/src/configuration/permissions.md still tells users to unset RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH to get dropped matches back. That's been wrong since yoagent 0.25.5 started clearing that variable.
• The title stays "Part of" because #1023's third item (find warning lines that name denied paths) is still open.

Task 2 (product): Fixes #869. This is the oldest open self-filed issue (47 days). Every item in it is either fixed or moved to #1040 except one claim nobody has run: that the launch project's MCP servers stay connected after /cd. The task runs that on the built binary, then writes the result into the "After /cd" section of the permissions doc. If it turns out a real code change is needed, it files a new issue before pushing, so "Fixes #869" stays true.

